    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -580,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        760
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Anima Komikku · Char Ref (Anima Ref Adapter)\n\nOne Anima prompt per manga panel. **Page & Panels** outputs a list of prompts and panel sizes, so the single sampler chain renders every panel in panel order; **Page Compose** frames and letters the page.\n\n**Character identity: Anima Ref Adapter** (anima_ref_adapter_v2_r64), up to two characters. Load them in Character 1 (left) and Character 2 (right); Image Stitch puts them side by side. In each panel prompt, name who is there by a few appearance words: `2girls, the girl on the left is ..., the girl on the right is ...` for both, or `1girl, solo, the girl with ...` for one. For a one-character page, bypass Image Stitch (Ctrl+B). The adapter keeps the characters close but also brings the pictures' drawing style; ref_guidance above 1 costs one extra model call per step.\n\n**Global style** (pick one):\n- **Anima Artist Mixer**: artists in *artist_chain*, mixed per artist without prompt interference.\n- **Style tags**: empty *artist_chain* and write the artist tags (e.g. @artist) in *style* on Page & Panels.\n\nPanel prompts are Danbooru tags: count (1girl, solo), framing (close-up, cowboy shot, wide shot, from below), then pose, place, light. Never name the character; a few appearance words only to tell the two characters apart.\n\nModel: **mangaVisionANIIL_animaV1** (Anima manga finetune), er_sde, 30 steps, cfg 4.5. Add Anima LoRAs in the **Power Lora Loader**; style LoRAs add to the artist style."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Anima Komikku · Char Ref (Anima Ref Adapter)\n\nOne Anima prompt per manga panel. **Page & Panels** outputs a list of prompts and panel sizes, so the single sampler chain renders every panel in panel order; **Page Compose** frames and letters the page.\n\n**Character identity: Anima Ref Adapter** (anima_ref_adapter_v2_r64), up to two characters. Load them in Character 1 (left) and Character 2 (right); Image Stitch puts them side by side. In each panel prompt, name who is there by a few appearance words: `2girls, the girl on the left is ..., the girl on the right is ...` for both, or `1girl, solo, the girl with ...` for one. For a one-character page, bypass Image Stitch (Ctrl+B). The adapter keeps the characters close but also brings the pictures' drawing style; ref_guidance above 1 costs one extra model call per step.\n\n**Global style** (pick one):\n- **Anima Artist Mixer**: artists in *artist_chain*, mixed per artist without prompt interference.\n- **Style tags**: empty *artist_chain* and write the artist tags (e.g. @artist) in *style* on Page & Panels.\n\nPanel prompts are Danbooru tags: count (1girl, solo), framing (close-up, cowboy shot, wide shot, from below), then pose, place, light. Never name the character; a few appearance words only to tell the two characters apart.\n\nModel: **mangaVisionANIIL_animaV1** (Anima manga finetune), er_sde, 30 steps, cfg 4.5. Add Anima LoRAs in the **Power Lora Loader**; style LoRAs add to the artist style."
      },
